1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,824
For a blind student, ‘as you can see’ can hide the explanation.

2
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:09,750
Earshot starts with one request: teach me my latest lecture.

3
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:15,532
It combines your Moodle transcript and lecture notes, then explains the visual references in words.

4
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:21,836
You can follow its progress, and open the activity log to see the individual steps.

5
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:26,750
Here, a diagram becomes a spoken explanation.

6
00:00:29,354 --> 00:00:32,013
The horizontal axis is wealth in pounds,

7
00:00:32,047 --> 00:00:34,300
and the vertical axis is utility.

8
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:39,012
The text keeps up when I change speed, pause, or jump ahead.

9
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:46,697
The full explanation is there to read, with the original course sources just below.

10
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:54,244
Save the audio, and take the explanation with you when the screen stays closed.

11
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:58,653
Earshot. Your lecture, in your ears.
